mixin () {
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Common Thread — Backend API\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis canister is the minimal Caffeine starter backend for the **Common Thread** app. It exposes no app-specific entities or operations. Its public surface is limited to:\n\n- the shared authorization mixin (`MixinAuthorization`), which manages caller roles and registration, and\n- the OQL `Expose` mixin, registered with an empty entity list because the app persists no queryable data.\n\nBecause no domain data is stored, there are no CRUD endpoints, no timestamps, and no polling or lifecycle state to observe.\n\n## Authentication\n\nAuthentication is provided by Internet Identity through the app frontend. The frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent that already holds the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n\nA caller is identified by the principal the canister receives; the canister never trusts a client-supplied identity.\n\n## Authorization\n\nAuthorization is role-based and owned by the shared authorization mixin. Roles are assigned per principal and enforced on the backend. Registration happens only when a caller signs in through the app's own frontend; a principal that never did so is unregistered even when it belongs to the app's owner, and a signed-in caller derived against a different origin is a different principal than the one the frontend registered.\n\nA direct API caller must register before any role-guarded call, guarded queries included, by calling `_initialize_access_control` once as a signed-in caller. The first initializer receives the admin role; subsequent callers receive the default (non-admin) role. An unregistered or anonymous caller on a guarded endpoint is rejected by the mixin's own trap message.\n\n## Units and encoding\n\n- **Principals** are Candid `principal` values; text forms are the standard base32 principal encoding.\n- **Roles** are the authorization mixin's `UserRole` variant.\n- There are no numeric units, timestamps, or blobs in this scaffold's own API.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\nThere is no asynchronous work, job queue, or state machine in this scaffold. Every call completes synchronously within its own message; there is nothing to poll and no completion condition to wait on.\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n\nRole assignment and registration are idempotent in effect: re-registering an already-registered caller does not create duplicate state, and assigning the same role twice leaves the same role in place. Retrying a call after a transport error is therefore safe.\n\n## Errors and gotchas\n\n- Guarded endpoints reject unregistered or anonymous callers with a trap; the frontend receives an opaque reject, so callers should register first.\n- The OQL `Expose` mixin is registered with `entities = []`, so `schema()` reports no tables and `execute()` has nothing to query. This is intentional for the starter scaffold.\n- No cycles are transferred by any endpoint.\n"
  };
};
